    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That metaphor makes sense, but I'm worried about the 'unknown' tag being too vague for our searchable database. If we have a lot of these 'anonymous' entries, it might mess up our authority control. Are there any specific controlled vocabularies or standardized terms (like Getty AAT or LCSH) that are better for marking an entity as truly unidentified or 'lost' to history within a Dublin Core framework?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
